title: COW-APPMENU
section: 1
date: @DATE@
source: @VERSION@
volume: cow - Window Manager

# NAME

cow-appmenu - discover installed desktop applications

# SYNOPSIS

**cow-appmenu** \[**--menu** \[*file*\]\] \[**--fallback** *file*\]
\[**--format** *json|cow*\] \[**--name** *name*\] \[**--terminal** *program*\]
\[**--icon-size** *pixels*\] \[**--help**\]

**cow-appmenu --launch** *file* \[**--terminal** *program*\]

**cow-applications** \[**--load**\] \[*terminal-program*\]

# DESCRIPTION

**cow-appmenu** writes a JSON catalogue of visible desktop applications to
standard output. It needs neither a running CoW instance nor a display.

Applications are discovered in the XDG data directories. User entries take
precedence over system entries, including entries marked **Hidden**.
**NoDisplay**, **OnlyShowIn**, **NotShowIn**, and **TryExec** control which
applications are included.

The output contains a **version** number and an **applications** array. Each
application includes its desktop-entry ID, source file, display labels, icon,
execution metadata, categories, and keywords.

With **--menu**, the output also contains a **menu** hierarchy. Menus have an
**id**, **name**, **applications** array of references, and a **menus** array
of submenus. Empty menus are retained; a deleted root produces **null**.

Each menu also has an **entries** array giving display order. Entries have type
**menu**, **application**, or **separator**. Menu entries reference an **id**;
application entries reference both **id** and **file**.

Without a filename, **--menu** searches the XDG configuration directories for
**menus/${XDG_MENU_PREFIX}applications.menu**, with user configuration first.
If no file exists, it uses CoW's installed **applications.menu**. Use
**--fallback** *file* to select a different fallback for automatic discovery.
Existing but invalid menus report an error; they do not use the fallback.
**menu_file** records the chosen file and **menu_source** is **explicit**,
**discovered**, or **fallback**.

JSON version 2 identifies each referenced application by both **id** and
**file**, matching the corresponding catalogue entry. Different menu scopes may
use different files with the same desktop-entry ID.

This initial resolver supports nested menus, **Name**, **AppDir**,
**DefaultAppDirs**, ordered **Include**/**Exclude** rules, **All**,
**Filename**, **Category**, **And**, **Or**, **Not**, **Deleted**, and
**NotDeleted**.

**Directory**, **DirectoryDir**, and **DefaultDirectoryDirs** provide localized
menu names, icons, comments, and visibility from **.directory** files. Later
search directories take priority and are inherited by submenus. Relative paths
are resolved against the menu file. Missing directory entries fall back to
earlier references, then the menu's **Name**. Menu IDs remain independent of
translated labels.

Application search paths also inherit into submenus without affecting siblings.
Later directories override earlier ones, including hidden entries. Relative
paths are resolved against the menu file. The catalogue includes visible
default applications and custom applications considered during resolution.

**OnlyUnallocated** restricts a menu to applications not included by ordinary
menus. An application included and then excluded still counts as allocated.
**NotOnlyUnallocated** restores ordinary matching. The last flag wins.

**MergeFile** and **MergeDir** include local menu files. **MergeFile** accepts
an omitted type or **type="path"**. Relative paths in included files retain
their original base directory. Same-named submenus are combined, preserving
directive order. Missing includes are ignored; malformed files and recursive
includes are errors.

**type="parent"** ignores the element's text and searches the remaining XDG
configuration directories for the same menu filename. **DefaultMergeDirs**
includes the corresponding **menus/*name*-merged** directories, applying user
fragments last. For the prefixed applications menu, the name is
**applications-merged**.

**Layout** and inherited **DefaultLayout** support **Filename**, **Menuname**,
**Separator**, and **Merge** with type **menus**, **files**, or **all**.
Explicit entries retain their positions; merged entries are sorted by display
label. Without a layout, submenus precede applications. Empty submenus are
omitted from **entries** unless **show_empty="true"** is set. The membership
arrays are unchanged. Leading, trailing, and repeated separators are omitted.

**Move** supports pairs of **Old** and **New** menu paths, relative to their
containing menu. Child moves run first, then parent moves in document order.
Missing sources are ignored; missing destinations are created. Existing
destinations are merged with the moved menu, retaining destination precedence.
Moving a menu into its own descendants is rejected.

**inline="true"** places small submenus directly in their parent.
**inline_limit** defaults to four entries; zero removes the limit.
**inline_header** controls the heading, and **inline_alias** uses the menu's
name for a single entry instead. These attributes may be set on
**DefaultLayout** or overridden on **Menuname**.

Unsupported elements and attributes are reported as errors. This is not a
complete XDG Menu implementation.

# LAUNCHING

**--launch** reads a desktop entry and replaces the helper with its program.
Arguments are parsed using desktop-entry quoting, not shell syntax. **Path**
selects the working directory. **%c**, **%k**, **%i**, and **%%** are expanded;
file/URL placeholders are removed because this launcher opens applications
without documents. Invalid field codes and quoting are errors.

For **Terminal=true**, **--terminal** selects an executable accepting **-e
command arguments...**; it defaults to **xterm**. This option is a program name
or path, not a shell command. D-Bus-only activation and startup notification
are not implemented. Entries with **DBusActivatable=true** can still launch
when they supply an **Exec** fallback.

Only launch desktop entries you trust: they specify executable programs.

# COW MENU OUTPUT

With **--menu --format cow**, the helper emits configuration commands instead
of JSON. **--name** selects the root menu name, defaulting to **Applications**.
Generated submenus use names beneath that prefix; reserve it for the helper.
Repeated loads replace menu contents rather than appending duplicate entries.
Removed categories may leave unused menu definitions until CoW restarts.

Every menu enables typeahead. An **All applications** submenu provides a flat
search across the applications included in the hierarchy. Selecting an
application runs **cow-appmenu --launch**, passing **--terminal** through. The
installed helper must be available on **PATH**.

Unsupported launch entries and entries whose executable is missing appear
disabled, with diagnostics on standard error. Empty menus show an explanatory
message instead of a blank list. Refresh the menu after installing applications.
Application and submenu icons use CoW's shared **hicolor** and **pixmaps**
lookup in the XDG data directories. Readable absolute PNG, SVG, and XPM paths
are also accepted. Missing icons leave text-only entries. Other themes and
**index.theme** inheritance are not supported yet.

**--icon-size** selects the lookup size (1–1024 pixels, default 16). It does
not change the menu's rendered icon size; use **menu-style icon.size** for
that. Lookups, including misses, are cached during generation. The helper
locates files; CoW validates and renders them when the menu is loaded.
Generating output neither loads it into CoW nor starts programs.

# DEFAULT LAUNCHER

**cow-applications** generates a menu, loads it through **moocow**, and opens
it centred on the current output. **--load** only populates the menu without
opening it. CoW runs this mode in the background at startup and restart,
through the **applications-refresh** alias. The root menu opens the result as a
normal submenu. Each helper invocation rescans installed applications.

Refresh failures show a brief notification; run **cow-applications** in a
terminal for detailed diagnostics. Failed generation leaves the previous menu
unchanged.

The optional argument selects the terminal executable. Otherwise,
**cow-terminal** chooses **foot**, then **xterm**, from **PATH** when launching
an entry. Without either, non-terminal applications remain usable but terminal
entries require installing a terminal.

The generated **CoWApplications** menu namespace belongs to this launcher. Your
root menu and any separately defined **Applications** menu are untouched.
Generation errors leave the existing menu unchanged. A private temporary file
is removed after loading. **WAYLAND_DISPLAY** selects the running session as
usual; the helper needs **cow-appmenu** and **moocow** installed on **PATH**.

Override the default launcher in **~/.config/cow/cow.conf**, for example:

```text
alias applications-refresh exec cow-applications --load foot
```

Use **alias applications-refresh script { }** to disable automatic generation,
or replace the root menu to remove the entry altogether. Run **moocow
applications-refresh** to refresh after installing applications, or **moocow
applications** to refresh and open the menu directly.

# PANEL INTEGRATION

**cowbuttons**(1) reads the JSON catalogue to populate its **applications**
entries. Panel layout, appearance and embedded applications belong to the
cowbuttons configuration, not to this tool. Run **cowbuttons -S** to use the
shipped starter panel, or copy its configuration to customise it.

# ENVIRONMENT

**XDG_CONFIG_HOME**, **XDG_CONFIG_DIRS**

: User and system configuration directories; default to **$HOME/.config**
  and **/etc/xdg**, respectively.

**XDG_MENU_PREFIX**

: Prefix of the applications menu filename, such as **cow-**. Defaults to
  empty.

**XDG_DATA_HOME**

: User data directory; defaults to **$HOME/.local/share**.

**XDG_DATA_DIRS**

: Colon-separated system data directories; defaults to
  **/usr/local/share:/usr/share**.

**XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP**

: Colon-separated desktop names used for visibility checks. Defaults to
  **CoW**.

**LC_ALL**, **LC_MESSAGES**, **LANG**

: Select translated display labels, in that order of precedence.

**PATH**

: Used to locate programs named by **TryExec**.

# NOTES

**Exec** is desktop-entry syntax, not a shell command. **Exec**,
**Categories**, and **Keywords** retain their desktop-entry escaping. Consumers
must interpret those fields before using them. Icons may be theme names rather
than filesystem paths.

Directory symlinks are not traversed. File symlinks are accepted.

# EXAMPLES

Inspect installed applications:

```sh
cow-appmenu | jq '.applications[] | {id, Name}'
```

Resolve the example hierarchy from a source checkout:

```sh
cow-appmenu --menu examples/applications.menu | jq .menu
```

Generate a configuration file, then include its absolute path in **cow.conf**:

```sh
cow-appmenu --menu --format cow --terminal foot > applications.conf
```

Open the generated menu with **menu-show Applications**.

# SEE ALSO

**cow**(1), **cowbuttons**(1)
